If we observe the scripts closely, we will see some words that are repeating. For example cart.sh we have a word cart repeating multiple times. In case tomorrow if we need to change that word then we need to update it in many places. This becomes a challenge.
This problem is addressed with variables. Variables are also called constants in other languages. Variables are like declare once, use multiple times.
In simple words, If we set a name to a set of data it is called a variable.
Syntax
VAR_NAME=value
Example

#its all about reusability, declare and reuse it meaning the value at one place,

# Declare the variable
x=100
# Access the variable
echo $x
# Access the variable using braces. This is alternate way

echo ${x}
echo ${x}times # Useful in the scenarios like this.


Variable names are declared in different ways by people of different backgrounds.

OS Background : Prefer variables to be in all CAPS with Underscore. ( VARIABLE_NAME)
Java Background: Prefer variable to be in camel case. ( variableName )
Python Background: Prefer variable to be in snake case. ( variable_name )
